ting to  add more sample to get a i think we need  to get a better result but in most cases  that's not always the case especially if  you have a higher levels of moisture  content in the percent range for example  when it comes to  paste or samples that are pasty  again same sort of precautions you know  in terms of isolating from the  surrounding environment  stirring the sample to make sure you can  get the best possible homogeneity and  again using that sandwich technique to  really  improve the accuracy when you're dealing  with certain types of samples to get the  best repeatability as well  so something that looks like what you  see here a very even distribution of the  sample between two filter pads is the  ideal situation that you're looking to  have  when you're looking to test different  types of samples  and certainly uh one of the things we  always like to mention just to have  everyone keep in mind is that you know  we do support uh any customers that are  looking into performing these types of  testing and we realize that it can be a  challenge from time to time optimizing  that methodology so we have an  applications method development team  that works very closely with our  customers and our our field support team  to provide not only trial instruments  for testing in your laboratory but also  customer support around methods  development which we've done for  thousands and thousands of samples so  feel free to give us a call or shout if  you have questions or needs in this area  and we'd be happy to support you as well  with our with our application support  team  other than that you know i just wanted  to make sure everyone is aware that we  do have quite a few um information  available online on our website when it  comes to applications and solutions for  chemical testing environments both for  all types of laboratories and feel free  to check that out at the link here  and again we thank you for your time  today and i would say we're pretty much